Let the distance between the twro places is $x \mathrm{~km}$.

\therefore \quad A M=M B=\frac{x}{2} \mathrm{~km}

Time taken by the car to cover first half $(A M)$ with the speed of $40 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{h}$ is given as

t_{1}=\frac{A M}{40}=\frac{x / 2}{40}=\frac{x}{80} \mathrm{~h}

Similarly, time taken by the car to cover second half $(M B)$ with the speed of $60 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{h}$ is given as

t_{2}=\frac{M B}{60}=\frac{x / 2}{60}=\frac{x}{120} \mathrm{~h}

$\therefore$ Average speed of car,

\begin{aligned}
v_{\mathrm{avg}} &=\frac{\text { Total distance travelled }}{\text { Total time taken }} \\
&=\frac{x}{\frac{x}{80}+\frac{x}{120}}=\frac{x}{\frac{5 x}{240}} \\
&=\frac{240}{5}=48 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{h}
\end{aligned}

